      "side": 0,
      "message": "One disadvantage of this patch is that we lose compile time check to catch invalid states. We can define unsupported states as \u0027reserved\u0027 instead. \n\n#ifdef CONFIG_USBC_VCONN_SWAP\n\tPD_STATE_VCONN_SWAP_SEND,\n\tPD_STATE_VCONN_SWAP_INIT,\n\tPD_STATE_VCONN_SWAP_READY,\n#else\n        PD_STATE_UNSUPPORTED_10,\n        PD_STATE_UNSUPPORTED_11,\n        PD_STATE_UNSUPPORTED_12,\n#endif\n\nThis way, if they appear in the code by mistake, we\u0027ll still get a compile error (while we enjoy the unified numbering). \n\nTo make it more readable, we can do:\n\n        PD_STATE_10(VCONN_SWAP_SEND),\n\nand\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_USBC_VCONN_SWAP\n        #define PD_STATE_10(X) PD_STATE_#X\n#else\n        #define PD_STATE_10(X) PD_STATE_UNSUPPORTED_10\n#endif",
